title: 'Built and on main: commit 4f7e218f, view snapshots. Reviewed by a fresh subagent; three findings fixed, two declined.'
pid: e098a111-aaee-4486-9b83-b126d4c9ffe5
body: |2-
  The run folder's 'views/' holds, per view, the text the server last sent and the
  buffer of its last save, overwritten at each exchange ('server/view_snapshots.rs';
  'docs/api-and-formats.org', "Log files"). Checked on a scratch copy of Jeff's
  data: a diff view, a search and a save each wrote their files, and a save with a
  fold showed the fold in both. All cargo tests pass (428 in the library).
  Cost: 1.6 ms in the debug build for an 80 KB diff-view buffer whose save took
  2.9 s; at most a few MB per run (Jeff's busiest run opened 73 views).
  Review: fixed a file-name collision between search views (a test failed first),
  writes that two connections could interleave (now a temp file and a rename), and
  the docs, which now say that a refused save registers text the client never got,
  and that a run folder now holds private text and is no longer safe to attach
  whole to a public report. Declined: rendering the forest a second time for the
  snapshot (measured cheap, and it keeps the change to two calls in the registry
  instead of seven call sites), and a view sent without a view ID going unrecorded
  (rare, and it has no ID to name the file by).
  The two calls in 'server/types/views_state.rs' and the one in
  'server/serve/handlers/save_buffer.rs' sit in other owners' files; their owners
  should know.
